  <data name="System_NoticeImmediateApply" xml:space="preserve"><value>OpenGlass brings back the Windows 7 "glass" look for windows: blur, reflections, and colored frames.&#10;Glass Platform adds modern see-through glass for menus, pop-ups, and the taskbar.&#10;Below you can enable autorun and the context-menu item; changes apply right away.</value></data>
  <data name="System_NoticeBannerGlass" xml:space="preserve"><value>Glass Platform — global glass effects for Win32 application windows, plus menus, tooltip pop-ups, and the taskbar. It runs in the background alongside your apps.</value></data>
  <data name="System_NoticeBannerImportantBefore" xml:space="preserve"><value>Important: platform modules are loaded globally into all processes. This carries a certain stability and security risk. Unwanted or risky processes can be added to the </value></data>
  <data name="System_NoticeBannerImportantAfter" xml:space="preserve"><value>.</value></data>
  <data name="System_NoticeProcessesLink" xml:space="preserve"><value>Blocked process list</value></data>
  <data name="System_NoticeBannerOpenGlassBefore" xml:space="preserve"><value>OpenGlass is Legacy AeroGlass: blur behind the window; parallax movement of the glass glow texture (</value></data>
  <data name="System_NoticeBannerOpenGlassAfter" xml:space="preserve"><value>); custom window frame; glass color and transparency.</value></data>
  <data name="System_NoticeReflectionLink" xml:space="preserve"><value>textures</value></data>
  <data name="System_OpenGlassUpdateTitle" xml:space="preserve"><value>A new OpenGlass version {0} is available. Installed: {1}.</value></data>
  <data name="System_OpenGlassUpdateMessage" xml:space="preserve"><value>Consider updating OpenGlass to the latest legacy release.</value></data>
  <data name="System_OpenGlassUpdateAction" xml:space="preserve"><value>Download</value></data>
  <data name="Notice_OpenGlassBorderBody" xml:space="preserve"><value>Window borders are drawn by the Desktop Window Manager (DWM). When OpenGlass is active, it takes precedence over DWM and overrides border color. You cannot change border colors while OpenGlass is running. Stop OpenGlass if colored borders are important to you.</value></data>
  <data name="Notice_OpenGlassBorderTitle" xml:space="preserve"><value>Border color changes are limited</value></data>
  <data name="Notice_OpenGlassBorderTraySuffix" xml:space="preserve"><value>For the taskbar, it remains possible to customize colors in the XAML rendering path.</value></data>
  <data name="Notice_SwcaDwmBackdropTitle" xml:space="preserve"><value>Tint color limitation</value></data>
  <data name="Notice_SwcaDwmBackdropBody" xml:space="preserve"><value>The current glass backdrop type is a modern DWM Acrylic or Mica layer, which does not support gradient color changes, so you cannot set a custom color tint for the current effect. If a colored tint on windows matters to you, choose an effect from the SWCA category instead.</value></data>
  <data name="Notice_SwcaDwmBackdropBodyRootFormat" xml:space="preserve"><value>The current glass backdrop effect type in {0} is a modern DWM Acrylic or Mica layer, which does not support gradient color changes, so you cannot set a custom color tint for the current effect. If a colored tint on windows matters to you, choose an effect from the SWCA category instead.</value></data>
