  <data name="Text_InkWizardTitle" xml:space="preserve"><value>Text smoothing visual tuning wizard</value></data>
  <data name="Text_InkWizardPrompt" xml:space="preserve"><value>Choose the best text appearance (%d of %d)</value></data>
  <data name="Text_InkWizardNext" xml:space="preserve"><value>Next</value></data>
  <data name="Text_InkWizardCancel" xml:space="preserve"><value>Cancel</value></data>
  <data name="Text_InkWizardBack" xml:space="preserve"><value>←</value></data>
  <data name="Text_InkWizardHint_ForkRoot" xml:space="preserve"><value>Here are two fundamentally different ways to build the text alpha channel. On the left — single-pass (slightly sharper and more graphic), on the right — dual-pass (softer edge transitions, slightly less dense at the same gamma value because the gamma scale is doubled automatically). Pick whichever looks better to you — you will refine details within the chosen direction next; you can always go back and try the alternative.</value></data>
  <data name="Text_InkWizardHint_RefineCoarse" xml:space="preserve"><value>Gamma sets letter thickness: values above the baseline make the stroke thinner, below — bolder. The second row under each gamma option shows a contour preset already tuned to it — with contour on, you get a distinctive “printed” look that feels original. For clean smoothing without an embossed effect, pick the top row (contour off) on any gamma option. The next screen is another gamma refinement step in the same direction.</value></data>
  <data name="Text_InkWizardHint_RefineMid" xml:space="preserve"><value>Another gamma refinement step — differences are subtler than on the previous screen. Top row: no contour; bottom row: contour on with presets tuned to each gamma. If you turned contour on on the previous screen, or turn it on on this one, you will fine-tune the halo radius next.</value></data>
  <data name="Text_InkWizardHint_RefineFine" xml:space="preserve"><value>Final step — blending. This is the resulting density/transparency of everything you have already chosen and configured; it does not change thickness or contour — only the overall “weight” of the glyph with all effects applied. Pick what reads most comfortably on your background.</value></data>
  <data name="Text_InkWizardHint_RefinePseudo" xml:space="preserve"><value>Here you can tune contour properties — radius in the top row and intensity in the bottom row. Radius sets how soft the contour is — from a barely noticeable thin edge to a wide soft halo. Intensity under each radius option is already tuned so the effect feels equally strong regardless of radius — only contour softness changes, not how prominent it looks.</value></data>
